# The cascade baseline is BYTE-COMPARED by a test, so its line endings cannot
# be left to the checkout.
#
# cssSnapshot.test.js builds a snapshot in memory (LF-joined) and compares it to
# this file read as UTF-8. With core.autocrlf=true — the Windows default, and
# what this machine has — git rewrites the file to CRLF on checkout, so every
# line differs and the test fails. It passes immediately after the baseline is
# regenerated, because the test writes it with LF, and then fails the moment
# anyone checks the branch out again. That is exactly the shape of bug that
# looks flaky and is not.
#
# Pinned narrowly rather than repo-wide: `* text=auto eol=lf` would renormalise
# every file in the project in one commit and bury this change in the noise.
frontend/src/__tests__/__snapshots__/*.txt text eol=lf
